  "prefLabel": "Mec 803.01 Eligibility Requirements for Certification as a Water Treatment Technician",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 803.01 Eligibility Requirements for Certification as a Water Treatment Technician. The qualification for certification as a water treatment technician shall be:\n\n(a) Successful completion of a water treatment technician educational program described in Mec 805;\n\n(b) Successful completion of the examination as described in Mec 805;\n\n(c) Good character and professional competence as evidence by the documents required by Mec 804.03;\n\n(d) Having:\n\n(1) Worked as a water treatment technician trainee for at least one year and have taken and passed the examination described in Mec 805;\n\n(2) Having operated as a water treatment technician for at least one year as a certified water treatment technician in another state; or\n\n(3) Having operated as a water treatment technician for at least one year prior to January 1, 2024.\n\nSource. #13632, eff 7-19-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/mec800.html"
